KNOWNBUG
scalar-bit-select1.sv
--bound 1
^file .* line [0-9]+: expected a vector type, but got .*$
^EXIT=2$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^\[main\.p0\]
--
1800-2017 11.5.1 "Vector bit-select and part-select addressing":

  "A bit-select or part-select of a scalar, or of a real variable or
   real parameter, shall be illegal."

A scalar is a single-bit net or variable declared with no packed
dimension (e.g. "reg s;", "wire w;", "bit b;", "logic l;").  A
bit-select such as s[0] of such a scalar is illegal and must be
rejected during type-checking.

EBMC instead treats a scalar as if it were a 1-bit vector and accepts
s[0], reporting the property PROVED with EXIT=0.  The type-checker
already rejects a bit-select of a real with "expected a vector type,
but got real"; a scalar should be rejected the same way.
